{
  "title": "Six Questions Five Pathways",
  "story": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "Twenty-one of Marc's frameworks read together. What governs all of them, what is invariant across them, and the five pathways worth writing first.",
      "id": "480890fe5751d693"
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "text": "<svg style=\"width:100%;height:auto;display:block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 1053 818\"><rect width=\"1053\" height=\"818\" fill=\"#ffffff\"/>\n      <defs id=\"svg-defs\"><marker id=\"mk000000\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker><marker id=\"mkc53030\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#c53030\"/></marker><marker id=\"mkc05621\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#c05621\"/></marker><marker id=\"mkb7791f\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#b7791f\"/></marker><marker id=\"mk276749\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#276749\"/></marker><marker id=\"mk2b4c7e\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#2b4c7e\"/></marker><marker id=\"mk553c9a\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#553c9a\"/></marker><marker id=\"mk97266d\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#97266d\"/></marker><marker id=\"mk234e52\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#234e52\"/></marker><marker id=\"mk1a202c\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#1a202c\"/></marker><marker id=\"mk3b82f6\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#3b82f6\"/></marker><marker id=\"mkf59e0b\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#f59e0b\"/></marker><marker id=\"mk8b5cf6\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\"/></marker><marker id=\"mk7c3aed\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#7c3aed\"/></marker><marker id=\"mk6B4C9A\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#6B4C9A\"/></marker><marker id=\"mk5A635E\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#5A635E\"/></marker><marker id=\"mk0E5A4B\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#0E5A4B\"/></marker><marker id=\"mk8A5F10\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#8A5F10\"/></marker></defs>\n      \n      <g id=\"wardley-layer\"/>\n      <g id=\"lop-layer\"/>\n      <g id=\"lines-layer\"/>\n      <g id=\"edges-layer\"><g id=\"edge-e_poia_cond\" style=\"cursor: pointer; opacity: 1;\"><title>\ud83d\udccc The most general model of humans acting together feeds the condition on all use.</title><path d=\"M524.6206896551724,114 L605.8786422349053,179.45779513367378\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6B4C9A\" stroke-width=\"3\" marker-end=\"url(#mk6B4C9A)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"548.9390979603502\" cy=\"166.97649920300225\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/></g><g id=\"edge-e_bgte_cond\" style=\"cursor: pointer; opacity: 1;\"><title>\ud83d\udccc And so does Beauty, Good, Truth, Economy. Both, not either.</title><path d=\"M775.3793103448276,114 L694.1213577650947,179.45779513367378\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6B4C9A\" stroke-width=\"3\" marker-end=\"url(#mk6B4C9A)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"718.4397660702723\" cy=\"126.48129593067156\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/></g><g id=\"edge-e_c_when\" style=\"cursor: grab; opacity: 1;\"><title>\ud83d\udccc Settings and context are chosen, not given \u2014 which is already an ethical act.</title><path d=\"M526.9275250185794,201.7498752888717 Q353.7,183.10000000000002 169.76383951244287,345\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6B4C9A\" stroke-width=\"3\" marker-end=\"url(#mk6B4C9A)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"352.7990566184655\" cy=\"198.29009734243152\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/></g><g id=\"edge-e_c_why\" style=\"cursor: grab; opacity: 1;\"><title>\ud83d\udccc Purposes are where the crown bites hardest: an efficient answer to an ugly purpose still fails.</title><path d=\"M515.5856166152893,225.0477035149052 Q458.7,229.3 367.5680159256802,345\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6B4C9A\" stroke-width=\"3\" marker-end=\"url(#mk6B4C9A)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"458.95035054052937\" cy=\"228.48528606430762\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/></g><g id=\"edge-e_c_who\" style=\"cursor: grab; opacity: 1;\"><title>\ud83d\udccc Who is included, and on what standing, is a Good question before it is a design question.</title><path d=\"M601.1895421212415,249.21822365776234 Q563.7,275.5 554.5885167464115,345\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6B4C9A\" stroke-width=\"3\" marker-end=\"url(#mk6B4C9A)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"554.3282924012118\" cy=\"261.2274045082323\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/></g><g id=\"edge-e_c_hows\" style=\"cursor: grab; opacity: 1;\"><title>\ud83d\udccc Strategy chosen without the crown optimises the wrong thing well.</title><path d=\"M658.0157170923379,260.7367387033399 Q668.7,321.7 705.1886792452831,345\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6B4C9A\" stroke-width=\"3\" marker-end=\"url(#mk6B4C9A)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"658.1950110138033\" cy=\"337.0327417517937\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/></g><g id=\"edge-e_c_howm\" style=\"cursor: grab; opacity: 1;\"><title>\ud83d\udccc Mechanism is where 'true to the ecology it sits in' stops being abstract.</title><path d=\"M681.612058652202,254.0742422629077 Q773.7,367.9 877.5,374.29826795720834\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6B4C9A\" stroke-width=\"3\" marker-end=\"url(#mk6B4C9A)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"773.3765931683637\" cy=\"370.8664113826676\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/></g><g id=\"edge-e_c_what\" style=\"cursor: grab; opacity: 1;\"><title>\ud83d\udccc Outcomes are measured against the crown, not only against the plan.</title><path d=\"M691.6332103353961,251.24474061118224 Q878.7,414.1 1087.5,390.46880185861266\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6B4C9A\" stroke-width=\"3\" marker-end=\"url(#mk6B4C9A)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"880.6605930073763\" cy=\"397.2767125536623\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/></g><g id=\"edge-e_seq1\" style=\"cursor: pointer; opacity: 1;\"><title>\ud83d\udccc Time and place before purpose. Marc's extension of Meadows \u2014 context precedes paradigm.</title><path d=\"M222.5,380 L247.5,380\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#5A635E\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" marker-end=\"url(#mk5A635E)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"235\" cy=\"406\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/></g><g id=\"edge-e_seq2\" style=\"cursor: pointer; opacity: 1;\"><title>\ud83d\udccc Purpose before people. Who you need depends on what it is for.</title><path d=\"M432.5,380 L457.5,380\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#5A635E\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" marker-end=\"url(#mk5A635E)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"445\" cy=\"406\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/></g><g id=\"edge-e_seq3\" style=\"cursor: pointer; opacity: 1;\"><title>\ud83d\udccc People before strategy. Strategy without the stakeholders in the room produces a document.</title><path d=\"M642.5,380 L667.5,380\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#5A635E\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" marker-end=\"url(#mk5A635E)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"655\" cy=\"406\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/></g><g id=\"edge-e_seq4\" style=\"cursor: pointer; opacity: 1;\"><title>\ud83d\udccc Strategy before mechanism. Deciding how to build precedes what to build with.</title><path d=\"M852.5,380 L877.5,380\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#5A635E\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" marker-end=\"url(#mk5A635E)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"865\" cy=\"406\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/></g><g id=\"edge-e_seq5\" style=\"cursor: pointer; opacity: 1;\"><title>\ud83d\udccc And What comes last. Answering What first is the standard failure \u2014 it produces solutions nobody will carry.</title><path d=\"M1062.5,380 L1087.5,380\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#5A635E\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" marker-end=\"url(#mk5A635E)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"1075\" cy=\"406\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/></g><g id=\"edge-e_p1_q\" style=\"cursor: grab; opacity: 1;\"><title>\ud83d\udccc Systemic Problem Solving runs the whole nested chain, in order, with stakeholders present. Two to four hours.</title><path d=\"M608.6626389560174,526 Q430.7,358.1 222.5,373.2632191553043\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#0E5A4B\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" stroke-dasharray=\"8 5\" marker-end=\"url(#mk0E5A4B)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"428.0296489785978\" cy=\"374.26685574979535\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><a class=\"internal\" data-title=\"runs the chain\" href=\"/runs-the-chain.html\"><text text-anchor=\"middle\" pointer-events=\"none\" transform=\"rotate(21.6,426.1,386.1)\"><tspan x=\"426.0740532827604\" y=\"386.10643536540766\" font-size=\"10\" font-style=\"italic\" fill=\"#0E5A4B\">runs the chain</tspan></text></a></g><g id=\"edge-e_p2_crown\" style=\"cursor: grab; opacity: 1;\"><title>\ud83d\udccc Walking the Tetrahedron is not one diagnostic among several \u2014 it is the governing model used as a check.</title><path d=\"M222.0486725663717,701 Q472.4,468.8 470.2647943831494,114\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#0E5A4B\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" stroke-dasharray=\"8 5\" marker-end=\"url(#mk0E5A4B)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"436.26513677751086\" cy=\"451.2539781288396\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><a class=\"internal\" data-title=\"the crown, applied\" href=\"/the-crown-applied.html\"><text text-anchor=\"middle\" pointer-events=\"none\" transform=\"rotate(-67.1,425.5,446.0)\"><tspan x=\"425.4704287614586\" y=\"446.01238687730375\" font-size=\"10\" font-style=\"italic\" fill=\"#6B4C9A\">the crown, applied</tspan></text></a></g><g id=\"edge-e_p5_who\" style=\"cursor: grab; opacity: 1;\"><title>\ud83d\udccc Collective Action Assessment is the Who shelf applied to a real commons.</title><path d=\"M524.0461538461539,701 Q604.2,571 559.9319371727748,415\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#0E5A4B\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" stroke-dasharray=\"8 5\" marker-end=\"url(#mk0E5A4B)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"602.4602179647961\" cy=\"570.6364439889587\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/></g><g id=\"edge-e_p3_why\" style=\"cursor: grab; opacity: 1;\"><title>\ud83d\udccc Leverage points are a Why question: where would a small push do the most?</title><path d=\"M715,715.5263157894736 Q500.8,665.6 359.70588235294116,415\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#0E5A4B\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" stroke-dasharray=\"8 5\" marker-end=\"url(#mk0E5A4B)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"508.80760176369705\" cy=\"643.6193481578687\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/></g><g id=\"edge-e_p3_what\" style=\"cursor: grab; opacity: 1;\"><title>\ud83d\udccc And SPC closes it on What: did anything actually change, or are we reading noise?</title><path d=\"M920.2857142857143,701 Q1079.2,639.2 1166.388888888889,415\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#0E5A4B\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" stroke-dasharray=\"8 5\" marker-end=\"url(#mk0E5A4B)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"1073.3889369430042\" cy=\"626.0426431609237\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/></g><g id=\"edge-e_p4_what\" style=\"cursor: grab; opacity: 1;\"><title>\ud83d\udccc The 15 Ps land on What through Product, Persuade, Purchase, Provide, Protect.</title><path d=\"M1162.5981308411215,701 Q1239.2,568.8 1190.9745762711864,415\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#0E5A4B\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" stroke-dasharray=\"8 5\" marker-end=\"url(#mk0E5A4B)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"1237.5538799150297\" cy=\"568.5151568938745\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/></g><g id=\"edge-e_r1\" style=\"cursor: grab; opacity: 1;\"><title>\ud83d\udccc Routed to when the situation involves something held in common that is depletable and open to access.</title><path d=\"M568.7798165137615,604 Q536.5,619.5 511.81327800829877,701\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8A5F10\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" marker-end=\"url(#mk8A5F10)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"534.9694838023357\" cy=\"606.1965874384464\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><a class=\"internal\" data-title=\"commons\" href=\"/commons.html\"><text text-anchor=\"middle\" pointer-events=\"none\" transform=\"rotate(-59.6,536.3,618.1)\"><tspan x=\"536.3409997336074\" y=\"618.1179524630678\" font-size=\"10\" font-style=\"italic\" fill=\"#8A5F10\">commons</tspan></text></a></g><g id=\"edge-e_r2\" style=\"cursor: grab; opacity: 1;\"><title>\ud83d\udccc Cynefin says complex: cause and effect visible only in hindsight. Intervene without pretending to predict.</title><path d=\"M664.519615692554,604 Q696.5,689.9 723.8622754491018,701\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8A5F10\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" marker-end=\"url(#mk8A5F10)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"697.194135507777\" cy=\"701.1429865935071\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><a class=\"internal\" data-title=\"complex\" href=\"/complex.html\"><text text-anchor=\"middle\" pointer-events=\"none\" transform=\"rotate(58.5,696.5,689.2)\"><tspan x=\"696.4546704188317\" y=\"689.1657919561043\" font-size=\"10\" font-style=\"italic\" fill=\"#8A5F10\">complex</tspan></text></a></g><g id=\"edge-e_r3\" style=\"cursor: grab; opacity: 1;\"><title>\ud83d\udccc Cynefin says complicated: expertise applies. Design and engineering tools.</title><path d=\"M691.236559139785,604 Q856.5,760.3 1035,747.5185185185185\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8A5F10\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" marker-end=\"url(#mk8A5F10)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"857.4677507664629\" cy=\"747.9381216923219\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><a class=\"internal\" data-title=\"complicated\" href=\"/complicated.html\"><text text-anchor=\"middle\" pointer-events=\"none\" transform=\"rotate(22.7,858.4,736.0)\"><tspan x=\"858.4043063738562\" y=\"735.974724867245\" font-size=\"10\" font-style=\"italic\" fill=\"#8A5F10\">complicated</tspan></text></a></g><g id=\"edge-e_p4_loop\" style=\"cursor: grab; opacity: 1;\"><title>\ud83d\udccc Posterity abstracts what is universal and writes it onto the shelf, where it becomes the input to someone else's Pathway 1. This is how the whole system grows.</title><path d=\"M1098.763440860215,701 Q933.5,544.7 765,556.7654320987655\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8A5F10\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" marker-end=\"url(#mk8A5F10)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"933.2674562383127\" cy=\"556.7968995860737\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><a class=\"internal\" data-title=\"Posterity \u2192 new pattern\" href=\"/posterity--new-pattern.html\"><text text-anchor=\"middle\" pointer-events=\"none\" transform=\"rotate(23.4,933.0,568.8)\"><tspan x=\"933.0368178290091\" y=\"568.7946829615207\" font-size=\"10\" font-style=\"italic\" fill=\"#8A5F10\">Posterity \u2192 new pattern</tspan></text></a></g></g>\n      <g id=\"nodes-layer\"><g id=\"node-poia\" transform=\"translate(470,70)\" style=\"cursor: move; opacity: 1;\"><title>\ud83d\udccc The most general model of humans taking action together.</title><polygon points=\"121.2,22.0 0.0,44.0 -121.2,22.0 -121.2,-22.0 -0.0,-44.0 121.2,-22.0\" fill=\"#F3EFFA\" stroke=\"#6B4C9A\" stroke-width=\"3.5\"/><circle cx=\"136\" cy=\"-40\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><a class=\"internal\" data-title=\"Social Action Tetrahedron (Persons \u00b7 Ideals \u00b7 Orgs \u00b7 Action)\" href=\"/social-action-tetrahedron-persons--ideals--orgs--action.html\"><text text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"#2E1F4A\" pointer-events=\"none\"><tspan x=\"0\" y=\"-8.5\">Social Action Tetrahedron (Persons \u00b7</tspan><tspan x=\"0\" dy=\"17\">Ideals \u00b7 Orgs \u00b7 Action)</tspan></text></a></g><g id=\"node-bgte\" transform=\"translate(830,70)\" style=\"cursor: move; opacity: 1;\"><title>\ud83d\udccc Beauty = aesthetics/passion. Good = ethics. Truth = ecology. Economy = surplus.</title><polygon points=\"121.2,22.0 0.0,44.0 -121.2,22.0 -121.2,-22.0 -0.0,-44.0 121.2,-22.0\" fill=\"#F3EFFA\" stroke=\"#6B4C9A\" stroke-width=\"3.5\"/><circle cx=\"136\" cy=\"-40\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><a class=\"internal\" data-title=\"Beauty \u00b7 Good \u00b7 Truth \u00b7 Economy\" href=\"/beauty--good--truth--economy.html\"><text text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"#2E1F4A\" pointer-events=\"none\"><tspan x=\"0\" y=\"0.0\">Beauty \u00b7 Good \u00b7 Truth \u00b7 Economy</tspan></text></a></g><g id=\"node-cond\" transform=\"translate(650,215)\" style=\"cursor: move; opacity: 1;\"><title>\ud83d\udccc Marc Pierson, Models for Seeing Systems. This is a precondition, not a pathway.</title><polygon points=\"0,-64.80000000000001 212.5,0 0,64.80000000000001 -212.5,0\" fill=\"#EDE7F5\" stroke=\"#6B4C9A\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"166\" cy=\"-44\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><a class=\"internal\" data-title=\"All the models below these two must be informed by these or they will lead to no good\" href=\"/all-the-models-below-these-two-must-be-informed-by-these-or-they-will-lead-to-no-good.html\"><text text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"#2E1F4A\" pointer-events=\"none\"><tspan x=\"0\" y=\"-8.0\">All the models below these two must be informed by</tspan><tspan x=\"0\" dy=\"16\">these or they will lead to no good</tspan></text></a></g><g id=\"node-q_when\" transform=\"translate(130,380)\" style=\"cursor: move; opacity: 1;\"><rect x=\"-92.5\" y=\"-35\" width=\"185\" height=\"70\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#4A6FA5\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><a class=\"internal\" data-title=\"WHEN / WHERE settings, context\" href=\"/when--where-settings-context.html\"><text text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"#1F3350\" pointer-events=\"none\"><tspan x=\"0\" y=\"-8.0\">WHEN / WHERE settings,</tspan><tspan x=\"0\" dy=\"16\">context</tspan></text></a></g><g id=\"node-q_why\" transform=\"translate(340,380)\" style=\"cursor: move; opacity: 1;\"><rect x=\"-92.5\" y=\"-35\" width=\"185\" height=\"70\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#0E5A4B\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><a class=\"internal\" data-title=\"WHY purposes, motives, beliefs\" href=\"/why-purposes-motives-beliefs.html\"><text text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"#0B3B31\" pointer-events=\"none\"><tspan x=\"0\" y=\"-8.0\">WHY purposes, motives,</tspan><tspan x=\"0\" dy=\"16\">beliefs</tspan></text></a></g><g id=\"node-q_who\" transform=\"translate(550,380)\" style=\"cursor: move; opacity: 1;\"><title>\ud83d\udccc Ostrom gives this shelf its own spine: Origin (forming) to Performance (managing) to Survival (surviving).</title><rect x=\"-92.5\" y=\"-35\" width=\"185\" height=\"70\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#A0522D\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><circle cx=\"88.5\" cy=\"-31\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><a class=\"internal\" data-title=\"WHO roles, agency\" href=\"/who-roles-agency.html\"><text text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"#5E2F19\" pointer-events=\"none\"><tspan x=\"0\" y=\"0.0\">WHO roles, agency</tspan></text></a></g><g id=\"node-q_how_s\" transform=\"translate(760,380)\" style=\"cursor: move; opacity: 1;\"><rect x=\"-92.5\" y=\"-35\" width=\"185\" height=\"70\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#6B5B95\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><a class=\"internal\" data-title=\"HOW \u2014 strategy interventions\" href=\"/how--strategy-interventions.html\"><text text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"#3B3155\" pointer-events=\"none\"><tspan x=\"0\" y=\"-8.0\">HOW \u2014 strategy</tspan><tspan x=\"0\" dy=\"16\">interventions</tspan></text></a></g><g id=\"node-q_how_m\" transform=\"translate(970,380)\" style=\"cursor: move; opacity: 1;\"><rect x=\"-92.5\" y=\"-35\" width=\"185\" height=\"70\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#6B5B95\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><a class=\"internal\" data-title=\"HOW \u2014 mechanism design, implementation\" href=\"/how--mechanism-design-implementation.html\"><text text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"#3B3155\" pointer-events=\"none\"><tspan x=\"0\" y=\"-8.0\">HOW \u2014 mechanism</tspan><tspan x=\"0\" dy=\"16\">design, implementation</tspan></text></a></g><g id=\"node-q_what\" transform=\"translate(1180,380)\" style=\"cursor: move; opacity: 1;\"><rect x=\"-92.5\" y=\"-35\" width=\"185\" height=\"70\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#8A5F10\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><a class=\"internal\" data-title=\"WHAT outcomes, affordances\" href=\"/what-outcomes-affordances.html\"><text text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"#513809\" pointer-events=\"none\"><tspan x=\"0\" y=\"-8.0\">WHAT outcomes,</tspan><tspan x=\"0\" dy=\"16\">affordances</tspan></text></a></g><g id=\"node-p1\" transform=\"translate(650,565)\" style=\"cursor: move; opacity: 1;\"><title>\ud83d\udccc Heuristics fail, draw the graph, Cynefin-type it, six questions with stakeholders, AIC, BGTE check, route.</title><rect x=\"-115\" y=\"-39\" width=\"230\" height=\"78\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#E2ECE7\" stroke=\"#0E5A4B\" stroke-width=\"3.5\"/><circle cx=\"111\" cy=\"-35\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><a class=\"internal\" data-title=\"1 \u00b7 Systemic Problem Solving the router\" href=\"/1--systemic-problem-solving-the-router.html\"><text text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"#0B3B31\" pointer-events=\"none\"><tspan x=\"0\" y=\"-8.0\">1 \u00b7 Systemic Problem Solving the</tspan><tspan x=\"0\" dy=\"16\">router</tspan></text></a></g><g id=\"node-p2\" transform=\"translate(180,740)\" style=\"cursor: move; opacity: 1;\"><title>\ud83d\udccc The crown used as a check. Four questions, sixteen named places to look.</title><rect x=\"-105\" y=\"-39\" width=\"210\" height=\"78\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#0E5A4B\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"101\" cy=\"-35\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><a class=\"internal\" data-title=\"2 \u00b7 Walking the Tetrahedron\" href=\"/2--walking-the-tetrahedron.html\"><text text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"#0B3B31\" pointer-events=\"none\"><tspan x=\"0\" y=\"0.0\">2 \u00b7 Walking the Tetrahedron</tspan></text></a></g><g id=\"node-p5\" transform=\"translate(500,740)\" style=\"cursor: move; opacity: 1;\"><title>\ud83d\udccc The only method whose output is a disagreement. Independent assessments, then discuss green-vs-red splits.</title><rect x=\"-105\" y=\"-39\" width=\"210\" height=\"78\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#0E5A4B\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"101\" cy=\"-35\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><a class=\"internal\" data-title=\"5 \u00b7 Collective Action Assessment\" href=\"/5--collective-action-assessment.html\"><text text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"#0B3B31\" pointer-events=\"none\"><tspan x=\"0\" y=\"-8.0\">5 \u00b7 Collective Action</tspan><tspan x=\"0\" dy=\"16\">Assessment</tspan></text></a></g><g id=\"node-p3\" transform=\"translate(820,740)\" style=\"cursor: move; opacity: 1;\"><title>\ud83d\udccc For complex problems. 14 leverage points, then the numbers gate, then SPC.</title><rect x=\"-105\" y=\"-39\" width=\"210\" height=\"78\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#0E5A4B\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"101\" cy=\"-35\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><a class=\"internal\" data-title=\"3 \u00b7 Shared Understanding to Experiment\" href=\"/3--shared-understanding-to-experiment.html\"><text text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"#0B3B31\" pointer-events=\"none\"><tspan x=\"0\" y=\"-8.0\">3 \u00b7 Shared Understanding to</tspan><tspan x=\"0\" dy=\"16\">Experiment</tspan></text></a></g><g id=\"node-p4\" transform=\"translate(1140,740)\" style=\"cursor: move; opacity: 1;\"><title>\ud83d\udccc The 15 Ps. Ends in Posterity \u2014 the move from model to pattern, which writes a new page onto the shelf.</title><rect x=\"-105\" y=\"-39\" width=\"210\" height=\"78\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#0E5A4B\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"101\" cy=\"-35\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><a class=\"internal\" data-title=\"4 \u00b7 Inspiration to Implementation\" href=\"/4--inspiration-to-implementation.html\"><text text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"#0B3B31\" pointer-events=\"none\"><tspan x=\"0\" y=\"-8.0\">4 \u00b7 Inspiration to</tspan><tspan x=\"0\" dy=\"16\">Implementation</tspan></text></a></g></g>\n      <g id=\"triples-layer\"/>\n      <g id=\"drag-layer\"/>\n      <g id=\"eip-statement-layer\"/>\n      \n      <g id=\"opm-symbols-chart\"/>\n    </svg>",
      "id": "7ad21dc263d55997"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "## Two models govern the use of all the others",
      "id": "9c2dd98e42463791"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "> Beauty is the basis for using all the models. That is why I put it at the top along with the most general model of humans taking action together: the Social Action Tetrahedron. All the models below these two must be informed by these or they will lead to no good. \u2014 [[Models for Seeing Systems]]",
      "id": "ecf77a79a14fec2c"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "This is a precondition, not a pathway. See [[The Two Governing Models]].",
      "id": "7103dca40c6d4da1"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "## One structure runs through everything below",
      "id": "00ba74bc5d80f967"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "Under the two governing models, one structure appears in nearly every framework: the Six Nested Questions \u2014 When, Where, Why, Who, How, What.",
      "id": "91bd03201be1dab3"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "They are the ordered chain in [[Neighborhood Systems Patterns]]. They are the first node of [[Another Sequence of Tools]]. They are what [[Story Structure]] exists to answer in narrative form. They are the tag on every one of the [[15 Ps]]. They are the extension of Meadows, with Time and Place added to contextualize the twelve leverage points.",
      "id": "3e4361d4d586c177"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "> The Story Structure diagram places the modeling tools not in a linear sequence but in a topology organized around the Six Questions. This is the most important organizational insight in the conversation. \u2014 [[RCN Modeling Theory]]",
      "id": "ca928615c1f9bc34"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "So the shelves for the storefront were not invented. See [[The Six Nested Questions]].",
      "id": "0f5233da5a6e3c73"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "## The sequence is not a pipeline",
      "id": "7c05c0865890ef6b"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "> The sequence is not a pipeline. It is a progression of question types, and the tools are matched to questions. \u2014 [[RCN Modeling Theory]]",
      "id": "64cdfe7382b1cfb6"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "A step is therefore never \"now open the Graph Tool\". A step is a question you are now ready to ask, with a tool named as the instrument that answers it. Every pathway below is written that way.",
      "id": "c8b7df1dae3554c1"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "## The rest of it",
      "id": "ad13ff5e7cbe599b"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "- [[The Two Governing Models]] \u2014 the crown, and why nothing below it is neutral\n- [[The Six Nested Questions]] \u2014 the shelves, and the tools placed against them\n- [[Models and Patterns]] \u2014 the particular and the general, and the move between them\n- [[The Causal Ladder]] \u2014 where to go when lost\n- [[Four Kinds of Sequence]] \u2014 ontological, diagnostic, production, curricular\n- [[WHO Collective Action After Ostrom]] \u2014 the thinnest shelf, built out\n- [[Three Files One Relation Each]] \u2014 where skills, pathways and tools each live",
      "id": "112db8323d2b7750"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "## The five pathways",
      "id": "4a65c4bc3dc9da2a"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "- [[Systemic Problem Solving]] \u2014 the router. It chooses the other four.\n- [[Walking the Tetrahedron]] \u2014 the crown used as a check\n- [[Collective Action Assessment]] \u2014 the only method whose output is a disagreement\n- [[Shared Understanding to Experiment]] \u2014 for genuinely complex situations\n- [[Inspiration to Implementation]] \u2014 the long arc, ending in a pattern",
      "id": "c832b67e0d81d2b7"
    }
  ],
